                <pb facs="0487" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5508: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-09-12T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 12,
                                1924—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>154. Your 227, September 10, 5 p.m. You may orally communicate to Baron Shidehara
                    the essential portion of the first paragraph <pb facs="0488" n="374"
                        xml:id="pg374"/> of the Department’s 151, September 10, 4 p.m., down to and
                    including “developments in China.”</p>
                <p>You may repeat to Peking for its information the above mentioned first paragraph
                    of the Department’s 151.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
